      "translatedText": "* `argc` Indicates the number of command\\-line arguments, usually at least 1, because the path of the program itself is also counted as an argument\\.\n* `argv` Indicates the array of command\\-line arguments,`argv[0]` is usually the path or name of the program itself,`argv[1]` Only then do the arguments passed in by the user begin\\.\n* `char* argv[]` It can also be written as `char** argv`; here both express the same meaning\\.",
